WEBVTT

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.850
The spaceship was very far away from home.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.850
I thought it would be a good idea, right
after Saturn,

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:13.050
to make it take a last look towards home.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.550
From Saturn, the Earth would appear very
small

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:19.050
for the Voyager to catch any detail.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.050
Our planet would be just a point of light.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.050
A solitary pixel, hardly distinguishable

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:30.050
from many other points of light that the
Voyager would see.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:33.050
Close planets, only distant.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.050
But precisely because of this imprecision

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.050
of our world thus revealed,

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.050
it would be worth having such a photo.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.050
It had already been well understood by
scientists

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.050
and philosophers of classical antiquity

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:49.050
that the Earth was a mere point of light

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.050
in a vast, cosmos-circundant,

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.050
but no one had ever seen it this way.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:58.050
Here was our first chance

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.050
and perhaps our last in the next decades.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:04.050
So here it is, a square mosaic

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:06.050
spread over the planets

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.050
and a foundation of distant stars.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:12.050
Because of the reflection of the sunlight

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:15.050
on the spaceship, the Earth seems to be
supported

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.050
in a ray of sunlight.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.050
As if there were some special importance

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.050
for this small world,

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:24.050
but it is just a geometric accident.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.050
There is no sign of humans in this photo.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:30.050
Neither our modifications of the surface

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:33.050
of the Earth, nor our machines,

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.050
nor ourselves.

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:37.050
From this point of view,

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.050
our obsession with nationalism

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.050
does not appear in evidence.

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:44.050
We are very small.

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:46.050
On the scale of the world,

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.050
humans are irrelevant.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:51.050
A thin film of life

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:54.050
in a dark and lonely torrent

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:56.050
of rock and metal.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:00.520
Consider this point again.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.520
It is here.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.520
It is our air.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.520
We are.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.520
In it, all of you who love it,

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.520
all of you who know it,

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.520
all of you who have already existed,

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.520
all of whom you have already heard talk,

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.520
have lived their lives.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:21.520
The totality of our joys and sorrows,

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.520
thousands of religions,

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.520
ideologies and economic doctrines,

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.520
each hunter and saviour,

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.520
each hero and coward,

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.520
each creator and destroyer

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.520
of civilization,

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.520
each king and plebeian,

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.520
each passionate couple,

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:42.520
each mother and father,

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.520
each hopeful child,

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.520
inventors, explorers,

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.520
each educator,

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.520
each corrupt politician,

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.520
each superstar,

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.520
each supreme leader,

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.520
each saint and sinner

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.520
in the history of our species

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:00.520
lived there,

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:02.520
in a large suspended tower,

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.520
in a ray of sun.

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.520
The Earth

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.520
is a very small stage

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.520
in an immense cosmic sand.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.520
Think of the endless cruelty

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.520
inflicted by the inhabitants

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.520
of a corner of this pixel,

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.520
in the almost imperceptible

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.520
inhabitants of another corner,

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.520
how often their misunderstandings,

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:26.520
how often their anxieties

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.520
kill each other

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.520
and how fervently

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.520
they hate each other.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.520
Think of the rivers of blood

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.520
and tears,

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.520
for all those generals

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.520
and emperors,

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.520
so that in their glory and triumph

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.520
they could become

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.520
the momentary masters

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.520
of a fraction of a point.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.520
Our attitudes,

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.520
our high imaginary importance,

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.520
the illusion that we have

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.520
a privileged position

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.520
in the universe,

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.520
is challenged

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.520
by this pale point of light.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.520
Our planet

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.520
is a solitary species,

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.520
in the great

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.520
and involving cosmic darkness.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.520
In our darkness,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.520
in all this vastness,

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.520
there is no indication

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.520
that helps us to come

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.520
from another place

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.520
to save ourselves.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:26.520
Earth is the only known world

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:28.520
to this day

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.520
that hosts life.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.520
There is no other,

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.520
at least in the near future

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.520
where our species can immigrate

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:38.520
visit,

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.520
sit down,

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.520
not yet,

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.520
liking or not,

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.520
having to stay.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.520
It has been said of astronomy

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.520
as a creative experience

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.520
of firmness and humility.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.520
There may not be

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.520
a better demonstration

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.520
of the human tolls and vans

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.520
than this distant image

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.520
of our thousandth world.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.520
For me,

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.520
it set our responsibility

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.520
to bring us more lovingly

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.520
one for one another

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.520
and to protect us

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.520
the pale blue dot

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.520
the only one

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.520
that we know.

